    ),
    paste0(
        "\u2022 Panel regressions with interaction terms across 53 countries<br>",
        "\u2022 Monthly FAO commodity indices & national food CPI, ~2000\u20132022 (public)<br>",
        "\u2022 **Lags: Yes** \u2014 lagged commodity prices used as regressors"
    ),
    paste0(
        "\u2022 Response: Food CPI inflation (y-o-y)<br>",
        "\u2022 Predictors: Global ag commodity prices, local crop conditions, food industry development, net trade status"
    ),
    "Pass-through varies: better local crops \u2192 lower pass-through; less-developed food sectors \u2192 higher; net exporters \u2192 greater pass-through due to trade adjustments.",
    
    
    # 2
    paste0(
        "**2) Understanding the Resurgence of Food Inflation in 2025**<br>",
        "Bank of Canada (2026)<br>",
        "[Link](https://www.bankofcanada.ca/2026/02/understanding-the-resurgence-of-food-inflation-in-2025/)"
    ),
    paste0(
        "\u2022 Supply-chain cost decomposition into 8 cost categories<br>",
        "\u2022 StatCan supply-use tables & CPI food, 2020\u20132025 (public)<br>",
        "\u2022 **Lags: Yes** \u2014 6\u20139 month lag confirmed from costs to retail food prices"
    ),
    paste0(
        "\u2022 Response: Food CPI (food at stores, y-o-y)<br>",
        "\u2022 Predictors: Imports, energy, labour, domestic goods, taxes, trade margins"
